<br/>
<h3>Siri AI Settlement Website Now Live: Apple to Pay Some iPhone Owners</h3><br/>
In May, Apple agreed to pay &#36;250 million to settle a U.S. class action lawsuit over Siri AI's delayed launch, and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/20/siri-ai-settlement-website-now-live/">the settlement website is now live</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2025/03/iOS-18-Siri-Personal-Context.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-994536" /><br/>
Apple will pay an estimated &#36;25 per eligible iPhone to eligible customers, who can submit a claim via the settlement website between September 21 and December 21 of this year. The exact payment may be higher or lower than &#36;25 depending on the total number of valid claims submitted and other factors, with the maximum amount set at &#36;95.<br/>
<br/>
Apple denies all of the allegations made in the lawsuit, but agreed to the settlement to avoid the costs and risks of a trial.<br/>
<br/>
<h3>iPhone 18 Pro Max Requires 'Prepare to Ship' Battery Drain Before Shipping</h3><br/>
The iPhone 18 Pro Max has a single-cell battery capacity over 20 watt-hours, which means there are additional shipping requirements. If an ‌iPhone 18 Pro‌ Max needs to be shipped somewhere, its <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/18/iphone-18-pro-max-shipping-restriction/">maximum battery capacity has to be limited through firmware</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/iphone-18-pro-max-prepare.jpg" alt="" width="1769" height="995" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1066237" /><br/>
According to Apple, the ‌iPhone 18 Pro‌ Max uses an "innovative battery-firmware solution" that limits battery capacity to below 20Wh between when the iPhone is manufactured and its delivery to a customer. Activating the iPhone removes the limit to make the battery's full charging capacity available.<br/>
<br/>
Customers who need to ship the ‌iPhone 18 Pro‌ Max for repair, trade-in, or other purposes have to use a new Prepare to Ship feature. Prepare to Ship discharges the battery to below 20Wh and sets a charge limit so the iPhone stays below the threshold during the shipping process.<br/>
<br/>
<h3>Apple Exec Says 'Hold Us Accountable' on iPhone Duo Crease</h3><br/>
Apple hardware engineering VP Tom Marieb recently spoke with TechRadar and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/19/apple-exec-iphone-crease/">shared some candid thoughts about Apple's upcoming iPhone Duo</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/iPhone-Duo-Open-large-scaled.png" alt="" width="2560" height="1440" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1063634" /><br/>
The ‌iPhone Duo‌ uses a matte nano-texture display, which is meant to cut down on glare and minimize the visibility of the crease. When asked if the ‌iPhone Duo‌'s crease would be more visible over time, as that's what tends to happen on other foldables, Marieb said the nano-texture display would help. He asked people to hold the company "accountable" on crease visibility.<br/>
<br/>
Marieb also discussed the Duo's innovative hinge, the use of Ceramic Shield 2 on the front display, and more.<br/>
<br/>
<h3>Beats 360 Deliver Customizability and a Revamped Over-Ear Headphone Design</h3><br/>
After months of teases and leaks, Apple's Beats brand <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/22/beats-360-headphone-launch/">officially announced its new Beats 360 headphone this week</a>. Priced at &#36;349.99, Beats 360 represents a rethinking of the Beats over-ear headphone design, with an emphasis on sound quality, comfort, and customizability.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/Beats-360-Hands-On-Thumb-2.jpg" alt="" width="1920" height="1080" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1066679" /><br/>
Beats 360 is not a replacement for the brand's Studio Pro over-ear headphone, as the Studio Pro will remain part of the Beats lineup at a reduced price point of &#36;299.99, down from the previous &#36;349.99. Compared to Studio Pro, Beats 360 features a completely new acoustic architecture that delivers up to 1.75× more active noise cancellation and a 12dB increase in output while maintaining clarity across all frequencies with low distortion.<br/>
<br/>
Swappable ear and headband cushions let you customize your look by mixing and matching colors and materials, with Beats offering <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/22/beats-360-pre-orders-open-amazon/">extra cushion kits at heavily discounted prices</a> as part of a launch promo.<br/>
<br/>
<h3>iPhone 20 Pro Display Sizes Leak Ahead of 2027 Launch</h3><br/>
Apple's 20th-anniversary iPhone lineup coming next year <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/21/iphone-20-pro-display-sizes-leak/">could feature slightly larger displays</a> than the iPhone 18 Pro models, if a recent leak shared on Weibo is accurate.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/01/Mostly-Screen-iPhone-Purple-Feature-2027.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1033225" /><br/>
Prolific Chinese leaker Digital Chat Station claims that early iPhone 20 Pro display specifications include a 6.41-inch screen with a resolution of approximately 2,686 × 1,236 pixels, while the iPhone 20 Pro Max is said to have a 6.96-inch display with a resolution of around 2,912 × 1,340 pixels.<br/>
<br/>
For comparison, the iPhone 18 Pro and iPhone 18 Pro Max feature 6.27 inches (rounded to 6.3 inches) and 6.86 inches (rounded to 6.9 inches) respectively. Meanwhile, the iPhone 18 Pro and 18 Pro Max resolutions are 2,622 × 1,206 pixels and 2,868 × 1,320 pixels, respectively.<br/>
